From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] GPU page cache and unswizzle threads do no work when off

Two patches of T117 did work on the default path, with their switches off. A speed loss first
blamed on them was not confirmed (T116 re-run in the same hour gave the same fps as T119 and
T120), so this is tidying, not a repair:

- 0541 (EDEN_UP_GPU_PAGE_CACHE) declared `static thread_local std::unique_ptr<PageCache>` in
  MemoryManager::GpuToCpuAddress ahead of the switch test. A thread_local with a destructor is
  reached through a call on the PS5, and that call ran at every address lookup, the hottest
  lookup of the GPU threads, with the switch off as well. The table is now a plain per-thread
  pointer declared inside the branch the switch opens: nothing per-thread is touched without it.
  It is never freed (64 KiB for each long-lived thread that used it).
- 0542 (EDEN_UP_UNSWIZZLE_THREADS) turned the unswizzle loop into a closure that both the helper
  threads and the caller ran, so the compiler reloaded the loop's values after every copied pixel
  (a byte store may alias what a closure holds by reference). With neither helpers nor 16-byte
  units asked for, SwizzleImpl now runs the loops exactly as they were before 0542. The helper
  and unit paths are functions of their own with every value passed by value.

Checked off the console: the new file against the pre-0542 code in 43,450 cases (full copies of
1, 4, 8, 12 and 16-byte pixels in both directions, switches off, units, helper threads and both;
6,000 random sub-rectangles), built with address and undefined-behaviour checks: 0 differ.

